@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="sv-card mt-4">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="fs-5">
        Solvia is a demo built for the PayPal AI Hackathon. Every student in
        it is fictional, every payment is PayPal sandbox test money, and no
        real student records are needed. Please use fictional details when trying it.
    </p>
    <p class="fs-5">
        The default AI reader is OpenAI's US-developed GPT-OSS 120B hosted by Together AI. Solvia sends
        your vehicle or schedule sentence to Together; the relevant page identifies that
        destination before you submit. Together serves the model on its own
        infrastructure. Its prompt storage is on by default, while training
        is opt-in. A US-developed model does not establish the processing location.
        We do not claim zero retention or a US-only processing region.
        Use fictional vehicle details without personal information.
        The operator can alternatively select Phi-4-mini through Ollama on the
        application host or a configured remote runner.
    </p>
    <p class="fs-5">
        Answers travel to the Solvia server even when a model runs locally
        there. API keys stay on that server. Solvia labels model versus rules
        output, and lets you review all fields before saving. The AI cannot
        set prices, approve payments or issue permits.
    </p>
    <p class="fs-5 mb-0">
        The public permit check (<code>/verify</code>) shows only what a
        parking officer needs — whether a permit number is valid — and
        never a student's name, email, or license plate. The college roster is
        public demo data, and the person switcher is for testing rather than
        authentication. PayPal processes sandbox payment requests separately.
    </p>
</div>
